# Accepted vulnerabilities. Each entry: why it is not reachable in how Argus uses the image, and
# an expiry that forces a re-check (the next collector pin, at the latest). Owner:
# security-architecture-reviewer (attests), cloud-native-platform-engineer (maintains).
# Added 2026-10-02, increment 1 review. Fixed only by an upstream release (ADR-0001: tools
# run unmodified).

# steampipe_export_aws v1.34.0 embeds pgx v5.6.0 (fixed 5.9.0): Postgres *client* memory
# safety, triggered by a malicious server. The export CLI connects to no database; Argus
# rejected the Postgres-backed mode (ADR-0012).
CVE-2026-33815 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-33816 exp:2026-12-31

# memgraph/memgraph:3.13.2 (and 3.14.0, checked 2026-10-31) bundles certifi 2026.7.22 under
# /home/memgraph/.local for its Python query modules (fixed 2026.10.18): the CA bundle trusts
# emSign roots with compromised keys. A CA bundle matters only to outbound TLS, and Memgraph has
# none: telemetry is off, the chart's NetworkPolicy gives it no egress, Compose puts it on an
# internal network, and Argus loads no Python query module (ADR-0044). Accepted by the owner on
# 2026-10-31; re-check at the next Memgraph pin, at the latest by the expiry.
GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 exp:2026-12-31
